xmake is a lightweight cross-platform build utility based on Lua.  https://github.com/xmake-io/xmake

### case1 (with xmake.lua in project)

This patch allows users to choose to use xmake to build c/c++ modules (contain xmake.lua) for lua in rockspec.

```lua
build = {
    type = "xmake",
    modules = {
        ["ltui"] = {
            sources = "src/core/lcurses/lcurses.c",
            libraries = {"curses"}
        }
    }
```

### case2 (embed xmake.lua string)

We can also embed a xmake.lua configuration.

```lua
build = {
    type = "xmake",
    xmake = "
        target('ltui')
            set_kind('shared')
            add_files('**.c')
    "
```

### case3 (builtin, without xmake.lua)

 We can also use xmake to completely replace the builtin build type of luarocks, and xmake will automatically generate a xmake.lua

```lua
build = {
    type = "xmake",
    modules = {
        ["ltui"] = {
            sources = "src/core/lcurses/lcurses.c",
            libraries = {"curses"}
        }
    }
```

### case4 (instead of luarocks/builtin)

I don't know whether it is possible to allow users to completely replace the luarocks/builtin build type through global configuration or environment variables? If so, how should I modify it?

```lua
build = {
    type = "builtin",
    modules = {
        ["ltui"] = {
            sources = "src/core/lcurses/lcurses.c",
            libraries = {"curses"}
        }
    }
```

like this?

```console
# use xmake instead of `builtin` build type
$ export LUAROCKS_BUILDTYPE=xmake 
$ luarocks install ltui
$ luarocks install LuaSocket 
```

